A||||5||spideyfoot||AC Compresser||||1||
Z||000000||spideyfoot||06-17-2001||11:21 AM||||I got my AC working and my serpentine belt came off Now I"m trying to decide If my compressor messed up and kicked off the belt I didn't  hear any noises or anything actually I went in the store and my wife turned on the Ac and radio with the motor off when I got back in no Ac and the car overheated real quick like. Should I just turn the wheel on the compressor to see if it is locked up or something||||reg||1
Z||000001||SteveJ||06-17-2001||11:37 AM||||Yea, its the old blame it on the wife routine. I've used it many times. Turning on the radio and AC with the engine off did not cause the problem. I'd put the belt back on and see if it does it again. <BR>You can, with the engine off, reach down and turn the compressor by hand. It dosen't guarantee it's good but will reassure you it's not seized.||||reg||1
Z||000002||spideyfoot||06-17-2001||11:53 AM||||yea I get her to come out when I work on the car so I can cuss at her feet when Im under the car. I get yelled at for every mess in the house though. That is of course done by the pets. Yea I didnt figure she could have had anything to do with it.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Carrolles||06-18-2001||09:59 AM||||With the engine off and the A/C belt off, turning the compressor by hand only tells you that the clutch is turning freely.The clutch has to be engaged to see if the compressor is siezed.||||reg||1
Z||000004||88CoupeV6||06-18-2001||05:32 PM||||If you turn the clutch by the outside, not by the pulley. if the outside turns free the compressor is not seized.<BR><P>------------------<BR>Josh <B>(known by TheFiero64 for first 1239 posts)</B><BR>     <IMG SRC="http://people.ne.mediaone.net/fiero64/Fiero642.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||1
Z||000005||cadaver||06-18-2001||09:49 PM||||Let me see if I can make this clearer to some one that doesnt know. <BR>There is a pulley on the compressor. This should spin very freely. The clutch it that weird plate thing that looks like it holds the pulley on. That should turn fairly easy. <BR>It could also be that the belt wasent tightened enough.<BR>Or for some reason the alingment it not right. I have seen it before.||||reg||1
